From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:21:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "drm/msm/a6xx_gmu: erhai: disable IFPC via
 erhai_no_ifpc param (fix silent POR on GPU idle)"

This reverts commit 9c3aa45c45fb.

The silent resets on GPU idle the original blamed on IFPC followed from the
mis-sized device tree windows (the RSCC at gpu+0x50000 outside the GPU
node's 0x40000 kgsl_3d0_reg_memory window, and the GX GDSC left unbound by
9c9eefdef1 because the gxclkctl node mapped only 4 KiB), which left GX
collapse and the RSCC handshake unmanaged; with the windows fixed the
catalog's IFPC idle level is used again.

The pre-revert text also carried an older MODULE_PARM_DESC(erhai_no_ifpc)
line with no matching parameter; it is dropped rather than restored.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750) with the whole series: the GPU
powers up at probe (no -19), the CX GDSC collapses on runtime suspend,
IGT msm_recovery gpu-fault recovers in 5 of 5 runs, and 2.5 h of desktop
use ran 3,227 runtime-PM cycles without a GMU wedge.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 32 ---------------------------
 1 file changed, 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 273baf303a9..baf99dc9bcc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -19,17 +19,6 @@
 #include "msm_gpu_trace.h"
 #include "msm_mmu.h"
 
-/* erhai: disable IFPC so the GMU FW never autonomously power-collapses GX.
- * Default ON (owner decision 2026-09-12, fix A) — the autonomous IFPC/GX
- * collapse is the suspected silent-POR trigger. Set 0 via
- * /sys/module/msm/parameters/erhai_no_ifpc to re-enable IFPC for A/B.
- * When set: idle_level is forced to ACTIVE and the GMU_OOB_PERFCOUNTER_SET
- * vote is held after each resume (same mechanism a6xx_gmu_sysprof_setup uses
- * to block IFPC for sysprof) so the GMU FW never enters IFPC. */
-bool erhai_no_ifpc = true;
-module_param(erhai_no_ifpc, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(erhai_no_ifpc, "erhai: disable IFPC (idle_level=ACTIVE + hold GMU_OOB_PERFCOUNTER vote). Default 1 — suspected silent-POR fix.");
-
 static void a6xx_gmu_fault(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 {
 	struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu = container_of(gmu, struct a6xx_gpu, gmu);
@@ -1402,23 +1391,6 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	/* Set the GPU to the current freq */
 	a6xx_gmu_set_initial_freq(gpu, gmu);
 
-	/*
-	 * erhai fix-A: with the disable-IFPC param, hold the perfcounter OOB
-	 * vote so the GMU FW never autonomously enters IFPC (GX power
-	 * collapse) while idle — same mechanism a6xx_gmu_sysprof_setup uses
-	 * for sysprof ("Perfcounter select register values are lost during
-	 * IFPC collapse ... use the currently unused perfcounter oob vote to
-	 * block IFPC"). The vote is cleared in a6xx_gmu_shutdown and
-	 * re-asserted here on every resume.
-	 */
-	if (erhai_no_ifpc) {
-		if (!test_and_set_bit(GMU_STATUS_OOB_PERF_SET, &gmu->status)) {
-			ret = a6xx_gmu_set_oob(gmu, GMU_OOB_PERFCOUNTER_SET);
-			if (ret)
-				clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_OOB_PERF_SET, &gmu->status);
-		}
-	}
-
 	return 0;
 
 disable_irq:
@@ -2341,10 +2313,6 @@ int a6xx_gmu_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 	gmu->idle_level = (adreno_gpu->info->quirks & ADRENO_QUIRK_IFPC) ?
 		GMU_IDLE_STATE_IFPC : GMU_IDLE_STATE_ACTIVE;
 
-	/* erhai: force ACTIVE idle (no IFPC) when the disable-IFPC param is on */
-	if (erhai_no_ifpc)
-		gmu->idle_level = GMU_IDLE_STATE_ACTIVE;
-
 	pm_runtime_enable(gmu->dev);
 
 	/* Get the list of clocks */
